{"round":"after-cycle-011","model":"Kokoro-82M v1.0","channels":{"war":{"file":"war.m4a","period":70.393,"level":-24.0,"digest":"fa1883b9308a7a2d","cues":[{"t":0.0,"d":16.55,"text":"UCDP counted about 244,600 people killed in organised violence in 2025, up from about 187,000 in 2024, and a record 65 state-based conflicts."},{"t":17.1,"d":9.65,"text":"SIPRI put world military spending at $2,887 billion in 2025, up 2.9% in real terms."},{"t":27.3,"d":4.8,"text":"Iran announced a prohibited zone around the Strait of Hormuz on 5 September."},{"t":32.64,"d":5.46,"text":"In mid-October, ship traffic through the strait stood about 70 percent below its pre-war level."},{"t":38.65,"d":6.58,"text":"Preliminary estimates put oil flows, with transfers at sea, at about 82 percent of pre-war levels."},{"t":45.78,"d":9.7,"text":"The IMF sees 4.7 percent inflation in 2026, hardest for energy importers outside the technology chain."},{"t":56.03,"d":12.51,"text":"In the Philippines, which imports about 98 percent of its oil from the Middle East, a state think tank estimated in April that 1.3 to 3.1 million people could be pushed into poverty."}]},"hunger":{"file":"hunger.m4a","period":34.902,"level":-24.0,"digest":"f0cc3ed4ed171121","cues":[{"t":0.0,"d":17.93,"text":"SOFI 2026 nowcasts 645 million people undernourished in 2025 (7.8%, range 608–696 million), about 14 million fewer than in 2024."},{"t":18.48,"d":14.4,"text":"Separately, 266 million people in 47 food-crisis countries and territories faced high acute food insecurity in 2025, 22.9% of those analysed."}]},"poverty":{"file":"poverty.m4a","period":50.473,"level":-24.0,"digest":"c140770ccab4b939","cues":[{"t":0.0,"d":22.62,"text":"The World Bank nowcasts about 811 million people, 1 in 10, below $3.00 a day (2021 PPP) in 2026; 2024, the latest year with sufficient data, stands at 824 million."},{"t":23.17,"d":25.12,"text":"UNDP and OPHI count 1.2 billion (18.9%) in acute multidimensional poverty in 108 countries, surveys of 2014–2025."}]},"inequality":{"file":"inequality.m4a","period":29.242,"level":-24.0,"digest":"0e6ef7f3dd8c2ff4","cues":[{"t":0.0,"d":11.6,"text":"World Inequality Lab estimates, 2025: the global top 10% took 53% of income and held 75% of wealth, the bottom half 8% and 2%."},{"t":12.15,"d":8.67,"text":"The top 0.001% held nearly 6.1% of wealth, up from around 3.8% in 1995."},{"t":21.37,"d":5.51,"text":"Average income in North America & Oceania is about 13 times Sub-Saharan Africa's."}]},"power":{"file":"power.m4a","period":35.676,"level":-24.0,"digest":"ad5955107e802860","cues":[{"t":0.0,"d":18.11,"text":"Forbes counted a record 3,428 billionaires worth an estimated $20.1 trillion at 1 March 2026 prices, 400 more people and up from $16.1 trillion in its 2025 list."},{"t":18.66,"d":14.48,"text":"Epoch AI estimates five hyperscalers held 71% of the world's cumulative AI compute in Q4 2025, up from 63% in Q1 2024."}]},"climate":{"file":"climate.m4a","period":108.15,"level":-24.0,"digest":"2828235ab53fb03f","cues":[{"t":0.0,"d":13.71,"text":"September 2026 was 1.63°C above pre-industrial and the 12 months to it 1.50°C; the month was the second-warmest September in Copernicus's ERA5 record."},{"t":14.26,"d":16.07,"text":"EM-DAT recorded 358 natural-hazard disasters, 16,607 deaths and 110.2 million people affected in 2025, figures still evolving."},{"t":30.89,"d":3.79,"text":"NOAA puts the central Pacific at 2.1 degrees above normal."},{"t":35.23,"d":4.59,"text":"A strong to very strong El Niño is likely into early 2027."},{"t":40.37,"d":8.9,"text":"NOAA puts the odds of a historic peak of 2.5 degrees at 83 percent for October to December, and 70 for November to January."},{"t":49.82,"d":6.51,"text":"It lands on oceans that set a September record, in a month 1.63 degrees above pre-industrial."},{"t":56.89,"d":4.41,"text":"COP31 meets in Antalya from 9 to 20 November."},{"t":61.85,"d":7.07,"text":"Current policies lead to about 2.8 degrees this century, full national pledges to about 2.6."},{"t":69.46,"d":5.7,"text":"The lowest path that overshoots 1.5 degrees needs cuts of 18 percent by 2030."},{"t":75.72,"d":1.79,"text":"The pledges deliver 5 to 8."},{"t":78.06,"d":3.49,"text":"As of July, finance and adaptation remained stalled."},{"t":82.1,"d":6.08,"text":"The Living Planet Index records an average decline of 73 percent since 1970."},{"t":88.73,"d":8.63,"text":"It rests on 35,803 population trends of 5,790 vertebrate species."},{"t":97.91,"d":3.43,"text":"95 percent in Latin America and the Caribbean."},{"t":101.89,"d":1.81,"text":"85 percent in fresh water."},{"t":104.26,"d":1.19,"text":"That is what is monitored."}]},"health":{"file":"health.m4a","period":85.632,"level":-24.0,"digest":"3a4d31242c726500","cues":[{"t":0.0,"d":13.82,"text":"UN IGME estimates 4.9 million children died before age five in 2024, down from 6.1 million in 2015, and the pace of decline has slowed by 61%."},{"t":14.37,"d":12.47,"text":"DR Congo's Bundibugyo Ebola outbreak reached 10,414 confirmed cases, including 5,372 deaths, by 30 October 2026 (INSP)."},{"t":27.39,"d":12.08,"text":"The Bundibugyo strain of Ebola in Congo: 10,274 confirmed cases and 4,992 deaths by 29 October."},{"t":40.03,"d":2.43,"text":"That is more than twice the cases of early August."},{"t":43.0,"d":4.42,"text":"Kenya has nine confirmed cases, and Nigeria reported one in October."},{"t":47.98,"d":2.47,"text":"No licensed vaccine exists for this strain."},{"t":50.99,"d":2.62,"text":"In Kenya, contact tracing is partly on paper."},{"t":54.17,"d":12.21,"text":"The EU and EEA recorded 1,715 West Nile infections by 7 October, the most ever reported there, and 130 deaths."},{"t":66.92,"d":9.76,"text":"Nigeria counted 18,334 suspected cases of diphtheria and 731 deaths by week 34."},{"t":77.23,"d":5.53,"text":"How much of this is climate, and how much is lost surveillance and vaccination, is still open."}]},"displacement":{"file":"displacement.m4a","period":50.726,"level":-24.0,"digest":"efbb6e68e0dda02d","cues":[{"t":0.0,"d":14.57,"text":"UNHCR estimates 117.8 million people were forcibly displaced at end-2025, 5.4 million fewer than a year earlier, with many returns under adverse circumstances."},{"t":15.12,"d":12.11,"text":"OCHA's plans list 252.8 million people in need in 2026; its global appeal was 44.3% funded on 1 November."},{"t":27.78,"d":8.38,"text":"UNHCR counts 117.8 million people forcibly displaced at the end of 2025."},{"t":36.71,"d":3.59,"text":"68.7 million of them inside their own countries."},{"t":40.85,"d":2.45,"text":"41.6 million are refugees."},{"t":43.85,"d":3.83,"text":"More than 1 in every 70 people on Earth has been forced to flee."}]},"democracy":{"file":"democracy.m4a","period":27.927,"level":-24.0,"digest":"7d513d5db0a5e429","cues":[{"t":0.0,"d":14.94,"text":"V-Dem's best estimate is 92 autocracies and 87 democracies at end-2025, with 74% of people (6 billion) living in autocracies, up from 50% in 2005."},{"t":15.49,"d":9.23,"text":"Freedom House recorded a 20th consecutive year of decline in global freedom in 2025: 54 countries down, 35 up."}]},"information":{"file":"information.m4a","period":55.165,"level":-24.0,"digest":"da8db4142e17cd6d","cues":[{"t":0.0,"d":14.67,"text":"RSF's 2026 index (covering 2025) rates press freedom \"difficult\" or \"very serious\" in 52.2% of 180 countries and territories, against 13.7% in 2002."},{"t":15.22,"d":10.15,"text":"In the 2026 Digital News Report survey, trust in news averaged 37% across 48 markets, the lowest since measuring began in 2015."},{"t":25.93,"d":8.27,"text":"By 29 October the Wesleyan Media Project had tracked 289 political ads made or enhanced with AI."},{"t":34.75,"d":4.38,"text":"Spending on them has passed 187 million dollars."},{"t":39.68,"d":3.19,"text":"In 2024 it was under 50,000."},{"t":43.42,"d":5.29,"text":"Of the first 220, 27 percent carried an AI disclaimer."},{"t":49.26,"d":2.52,"text":"No federal rule requires one."}]},"ai":{"file":"ai.m4a","period":71.416,"level":-24.0,"digest":"97634d65c38d2574","cues":[{"t":0.0,"d":9.25,"text":"The AI Incident Database recorded 362 incidents in 2025, up from 233 in 2024."},{"t":9.8,"d":16.52,"text":"US payroll data show no widespread displacement, but employment at ages 22–25 in highly AI-exposed occupations was about 19% below the pace of less-exposed peers by June 2026; descriptive, not causal."},{"t":26.87,"d":11.18,"text":"In American payroll data, employment of workers aged 22 to 25 in the jobs most exposed to AI stands about 19 percent behind less exposed peers."},{"t":38.59,"d":2.1,"text":"A year earlier the gap was 15 percent."},{"t":41.24,"d":2.26,"text":"It appears to come mainly from fewer hires."},{"t":44.06,"d":3.33,"text":"The authors call this a pattern, not a proven effect of AI."},{"t":47.94,"d":2.62,"text":"Where is skill learnt once the entry job is gone?"},{"t":51.11,"d":4.05,"text":"Data-centre electricity rose 17 percent in 2025."},{"t":55.71,"d":2.76,"text":"AI-focused data centres rose 50 percent."},{"t":59.02,"d":8.84,"text":"The International Energy Agency projects 485 terawatt-hours doubling to about 950 by 2030."}]}},"rest":{"file":"rest.m4a","period":150.0,"margin":0.3,"level":-24.0,"from":"2026-10-26","to":"2026-11-01","voices":8,"sample":{"labels":3647,"long":670,"stopped":98,"unreadable":346,"spoken":482},"cues":[{"t":0.94,"d":2.46,"text":"\"Liberals are the new racists\" ad","v":7},{"t":1.02,"d":4.58,"text":"Brazilian judge orders investigation into JD Vance donor network","v":4},{"t":1.24,"d":1.17,"text":"Andriy Lunin","v":6},{"t":1.64,"d":1.71,"text":"Cooper Pratt's World Series streak","v":0},{"t":1.86,"d":1.07,"text":"Zé Ricardo","v":3},{"t":2.09,"d":2.9,"text":"Tangled, hire a front-end accessibility expert","v":2},{"t":2.2,"d":0.73,"text":"Ritual","v":5},{"t":2.4,"d":1.57,"text":"Alexander Volkanovski","v":1},{"t":2.82,"d":1.14,"text":"Dilma Rousseff","v":6},{"t":3.54,"d":0.89,"text":"Gregory Peck","v":3},{"t":3.54,"d":1.27,"text":"clima dur